# Git & documentation

## Never commit

- `notes/` / `notes/**` — private AI/dev notes
- `local-packages/` / `local-packages/**` — local verify DMGs
- Secrets, `.env`, personal absolute paths, large sidecars unless the project explicitly vendors them

## Commits / push

- Create commits or push **only when the user asks**
- Prefer conventional style already used: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `chore:`

## Public vs private docs

| Path | Publish? |
| :--- | :---: |
| `README.md`, `README_KO.md`, `docs/`, `docs/ko/` | Yes |
| `notes/`, `local-packages/` | No |

- Product KO README is root `README_KO.md`; other KO docs are `docs/ko/<same-basename>.md`
- Policy/user-facing wording changes go in **public** docs; use `notes/` for internal plans/logs
- After a quality phase: update `notes/*` as needed **and** public CHANGELOG/README when user-visible
